children.desc:
The heat a body takes in (or gives out) depends on:

- its **mass**: twice the mass needs twice the heat;
- its **rise (or fall) in temperature**: twice the rise needs twice the heat;
- its **material**: 1 kg of water needs about **10 times** as much heat as 1 kg of copper for the same rise.

Put together: **Q ∝ m × ΔT**, and the material sets the number in front.

**Worked example:** warming 2 kg of water by 10 °C needs the same heat as warming 1 kg of water by **20 °C**.
